CLC management [Data: Entities (14330); Relationships (5906)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"阿帕替尼 exhibits distinct interaction profile involving CYP2C9\",\n            \"explanation\": \"阿帕替尼, another tyrosine kinase inhibitor used in oncology, demonstrates clinically relevant modulation of CYP2C9 enzyme activity. Published data show that阿帕替尼 exerts an in vivo regulatory effect on CYP2C9 exceeding 50%, indicating potential for significant drug–drug interactions with CYP2C9 substrates (e.g., warfarin). While阿帕替尼 also affects blood pressure and wound healing, its metabolic interaction profile differentiates it from吉非替尼 and warrants separate monitoring strategies, particularly in patients on narrow-therapeutic-index medications metabolized by CYP2C9 [Data: Entities (9074); Relationships (4674, 53227)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Multiple TKIs target NSCLC with varying development stages\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The community includes several tyrosine kinase inhibitors indicated for NSCLC, including吉非替尼 (approved), 阿帕替尼 (approved with extensive documentation), and 宁格替尼 (currently in clinical trials). 宁格替尼, developed by Guangdong Dongyangguang Pharmaceutical Group, is a multi-target TKI under investigation for NSCLC and represents an emerging therapeutic option. The presence of both marketed and investigational agents reflects ongoing innovation in targeted NSCLC therapy, though each carries unique interaction and safety profiles that must be contextualized within combination regimens common in oncology [Data: Entities (2577, 9074, 4281, 5062); Relationships (18871, 21023)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"EGFR-TKIs are classified under specific pharmacological categories\",\n            \"explanation\": \"吉非替尼 is formally categorized under both 'HER1/EGFR inhibitors' and 'epidermal growth factor receptor tyrosine kinase inhibitors,' reflecting its mechanism of action as a selective inhibito